    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "In CuPy v7.0.0a1, `**` operator calls `pow` function. https://github.com/cupy/cupy/blob/v7.0.0a1/cupy/core/_routines_math.pyx#L403-L417\r\n\r\nDue to the limitation of CUDA, computations results on the device may include error. Error bounds for each function are documented in the following page:\r\nhttps://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-c-programming-guide/index.html#standard-functions\r\n> pow(x,y) | 2 (full range)\r\n\r\nWe will change `**` to avoid using `pow`, so this behavior may change in the future (next) releases. (see #2204 for details)",
